# Supabase — Project Settings → API
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your project's values.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# Both values are safe to ship in the browser bundle: the anon key only grants
# what Row Level Security allows (see supabase/migrations/0002_rls.sql).
# Never put the service_role key in a VITE_ variable — it bypasses RLS.

# Anthropic (Claude) API — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Powers the "Lampara AI" assistant panel (src/ai/). Deliberately NOT a
# VITE_-prefixed variable: unlike a Gemini key, an Anthropic key cannot be
# restricted to a domain, so it must never reach the browser bundle. It is
# read only by api/agent.ts, a Vercel serverless function that proxies the
# Claude call server-side — set it in Vercel's project settings, not here.
#
# You only need this in .env.local if you're running `vercel dev` locally to
# test the AI panel (`vercel env pull` will fetch it for you); plain `pnpm
# dev` never executes api/agent.ts, so the panel's requests will 404 without
# it, same as they will locally until you've set this up.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key
